{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>As for Me, behold, My covenant is with you.</b> The expression 'behold' denotes something that already exists, so the verse means: My covenant already exists in you. And the truth is indeed so, for this outward circumcision is for an inner purpose — namely, that from it a proof may be drawn concerning the circumcision and purity of the heart. And without doubt, before this outward circumcision Abraham already had a pure and circumcised heart. Therefore HaShem, blessed be He, said to him: 'I know concerning you that already behold My covenant is with you, for you are pure of heart.' However, since now I wish to make you a father of a multitude of nations, I need to provide an opening for all who come into the world to understand why I am appointing you father of a multitude of nations. And this is to proclaim your merit and the purity of your heart before the eyes of all the peoples, by means of this outward circumcision that testifies to the purity of the heart — so that your generations may know that with justice I have made you father of a multitude of nations. This is what it says: ״וַהֲקִמֹתִי אֶת בְּרִיתִי בֵּינִי וּבֵינֶךָ״ — meaning, that covenant of the inner heart which was already hidden between Me and you, and of which all who come into the world knew nothing — behold, now I have raised it as a bannered flag of that covenant, so that all who come into the world may know it. And this is what it says: ״לִבְרִית עוֹלָם״ — meaning, that covenant which was between Me and you shall now be a covenant for the whole world, for all who come into the world shall know it and contemplate it."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:28:23.324946480Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}